<title>USA: Data networking stocks hit profit-taking bump.</title>
<headline>Data networking stocks hit profit-taking bump.</headline>
<byline>Eric Auchard</byline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading data networking stocks settled back for a round of profit-taking Tuesday after the strong price gains of recent weeks, securities analysts said.</p>
<p>After opening at a 52-week high of 67, industry flagship Cisco Systems Inc retreated throughout the day and was trading off 1-3/8 to 65-1/8.</p>
<p>Similarly, Cabletron Systems Inc and 3Com Corp began to fall immediately after Tuesday's opening. By mid-afternon, Cabletron had lost 1-1/8 to 67-3/4, while 3Com was down 2 to 70-1/8.</p>
</text>
